    "title": "When to Stream Hannah Montana's 20th Anniversary Special on Disney Plus",
    "text": "Two decades after the first Hannah Montana episode aired, you can revisit the hit Disney Channel show's stars, songs and fashion in a nostalgic streaming special. The Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special will soon debut on both Disney Plus and Hulu. It'll include an interview between podcaster Alex Cooper, the special's host, and star Miley Cyrus. The anniversary program will incorporate \"never-before-seen archival footage\" and recreations of the Hannah Montana closet and Stewart family living room, according to Disney Plus. It'll also feature a musical performance by Cyrus, familiar faces (Billy Ray Cyrus appears in the official trailer) and some surprises.Hannah Montana ran for four seasons between 2006 and 2011, giving rise to soundtrack albums and two films. Miley Cyrus starred as the series' titular pop star living a double life as tween Miley Stewart, and the cast also included Emily Osment, Mitchel Musso, Jason Earles and Moisés Arias. Here's when you can watch the new special.How to watch the Hannah Montana 20th Anniversary Special The new special premieres on Disney Plus and Hulu on Tuesday, March 24, according to a Disney press release. It's typical for Disney Plus to make new titles available at 12:01 a.m. PT (3:01 a.m. ET) in the US, and CNET has reached out to Disney to confirm the special will follow that timing.Disney Plus and Hulu standalone plans start at $13 per month with ads. The standalone ad-free versions cost $20 per month. You can also opt to pay annually for either ad-supported Hulu ($120 per year) or ad-free Disney Plus ($190 per year). According to Disney Plus, more than half a billion hours of the Hannah Montana catalog have been streamed globally on Disney Plus. Disney/CNET If you want your collection of streaming services to include both Hulu and Disney Plus, a bundle is probably the way to go. You can get a combo of ad-based Hulu and Disney Plus for $13 a month, or ad-free versions of the services for $20 per month. You can also peruse bundles that include HBO Max and ESPN.",
